BACKEND — pip-audit (venv-installed packages)
================================================================================

Command: .venv/bin/pip-audit --progress-spinner=off --format=json
Total packages scanned: 90
Vulnerable packages at the time of this scan: 3

Findings (installed version → fix version):

[HIGH]      pip                       24.0  → 26.2+
            CVEs: 2025-8869, 2026-1703, 2026-3219, 2026-6357, 2026-8643, 2026-13346
            Status: install.sh runs `pip install --upgrade pip` so deployed venv
                    is on the latest wheel; this finding reflects the local dev
                    venv only.

[MEDIUM]    langchain-core            0.3.86 → 1.2.22
            CVEs: 2026-34070 (GHSA-qh6h-p6c9-ff54), 2026-26013 (GHSA-2g6r-c272-w58r)
            Status: requirements.txt bumped to langchain==0.3.30 which pulls
                    langchain-core>=0.3.85 (still 0.3.86). The real fix
                    is langchain 1.x — ownership flagged in requirements.txt
                    comment, scheduled for Phase 2 (langchain major upgrade).
            Mitigation Phase 1: no untrusted LangChain config paths are loaded
                    from PDFs; CVE-2026-26013 (SSRF in Serper tool) is not
                    reachable — Serper is not imported anywhere.

[MEDIUM]    langchain-text-splitters  0.3.2  → 0.3.9 (minor) or 1.1.2 (major)
            CVEs: 2025-6985 (GHSA-m42m-m8cr-8m58), 2026-41481 (GHSA-fv5p-p927-qmxr)
            Status: requirements.txt pins ==0.3.11 which is >=0.3.9 — the
                    installed 0.3.2 is stale local venv; `pip install -r`
                    on deploy picks the pinned 0.3.11.
            Verify after redeploy: .venv/bin/pip-audit should report CLEAN.

