BACKEND — import smoke test (ran 2026-10-27 by support-impl-13)
================================================================================

Command: python -c "from app.main import app" + TestClient round-trips with
dummy env (APP_PASSWORD_HASH, SESSION_SECRET, MONGODB_URI, POSTGRESQL_URI).

Results:
  app.main imports                                            : OK
  GET  /api/health/status                                     : 200 OK
                        body={"ok":true,"service":"sevenlab-pdf","version":"0.1.0"}
  GET  /api/documents/   (no cookie, expect 401)              : 401 OK
  POST /api/chat/ask/stream (no cookie, expect 401)           : 401 OK

Observations:
  * fitz FutureWarning — deprecated import path still used somewhere; non-blocking
    (use `import pymupdf` instead per the warning).
  * Three routers mount at /api/documents/ (documents, document_mgmt, processing).
    Paths are distinct (/upload, /, /{id}, /{id}/status, /{id}/retry, /{id}/chat)
    so there is no FastAPI route collision — but path-param name is `doc_id` in
    processing.py and `document_id` in document_mgmt.py. Cosmetic, not a 500 risk;
    team should pick one.
  * Lifespan does best-effort pings to Mongo and ensure_all_indexes — both
    swallow exceptions so a bad URI logs a warning but does not block boot.
